{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"concepts":["feature scaling","tabular data","k-nearest-neighbour","accuracy"],"description":"The evidence from E2 focuses on the use of keypoints in stereo vision for KNN matching in spatial data, highlighting improvements in speed and accuracy of distance estimation. However, it does not address feature scaling (e.g., standardisation) of tabular data features prior to KNN classification. The context is specific to stereo vision and spatial distance estimation, not to tabular data with features on different scales. Thus, the claim about standardising features before KNN in tabular data is not tested or supported by this evidence.","evidence_ids":["E2"],"id":"G1","kind":"uncovered"},"hash":"abfb8e202927e37825840dcd99f91fc85e2262b5151eeb46556a21723a1af715","kind":"artefact","prev":"a913074d19b50a5bb33b805ee7df6dd8d42ea048e9be29dd980c5ac43338f88e","seq":19,"stage":"gaps","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:07.212+00:00"}
{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"concepts":["feature scaling","log scale","k-nearest-neighbour","classification accuracy","tabular data"],"description":"The evidence from E2 does not evaluate or compare KNN performance with and without feature standardisation in any dataset involving tabular data. The study does not explore how feature scale differences affect KNN accuracy in classification tasks on structured, non-spatial data. Therefore, the potential impact of standardisation on classification accuracy in tabular datasets remains untested.","evidence_ids":["E2"],"id":"G2","kind":"uncovered"},"hash":"0efb3dbdd1bd89e713ca66a723d028fcee9e76ee3796e7467fab62a8d4768f8d","kind":"artefact","prev":"abfb8e202927e37825840dcd99f91fc85e2262b5151eeb46556a21723a1af715","seq":20,"stage":"gaps","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:07.213+00:00"}
